{
 "fps": 30,
 "total": 18166,
 "xf": 18,
 "titleAfter": 5,
 "shots": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_01.jpg",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 413,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "July nineteen fifty-two. The night sky over Washington, D.C. Over the White House, the Capitol, and the most heavily defended airspace on Earth, something is showing up on the radar.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s01.mp3",
     "dur": 12.696,
     "start": 10,
     "end": 391
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_02.jpg",
   "start": 395,
   "end": 733,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Not one blip. Seven. Hovering, drifting, then jumping away faster than any aircraft of the day. Controllers swear the scopes are working perfectly.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s02.mp3",
     "dur": 10.176,
     "start": 405,
     "end": 711
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_03.jpg",
   "start": 715,
   "end": 1079,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Jets are scrambled. One pilot radios that the lights are all around him. A week later, the Air Force holds the biggest press conference since the Second World War.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s03.mp3",
     "dur": 11.064,
     "start": 725,
     "end": 1057
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_04.jpg",
   "start": 1061,
   "end": 1394,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Newspapers across America print the story. Then the Pentagon gives an answer. Hot air. A temperature inversion. Case closed. But was it?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s04.mp3",
     "dur": 10.032,
     "start": 1071,
     "end": 1372
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_05.jpg",
   "start": 1376,
   "end": 1842,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "I'm your investigator. Tonight we open the radar room tapes, weigh the evidence against the alien theory, and deliver a verdict. Let's start at the beginning.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s05.mp3",
     "dur": 10.44,
     "start": 1386,
     "end": 1700
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_06.jpg",
   "start": 1824,
   "end": 2142,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Summer, nineteen fifty-two. A heat wave grips the capital. America is deep in the Cold War, and the country is jumpy about the sky.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s06.mp3",
     "dur": 9.528,
     "start": 1834,
     "end": 2120
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_07.jpg",
   "start": 2124,
   "end": 2522,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Flying saucers are already a national obsession. In April, Life magazine asks if we have visitors from space. By July, reports are pouring in at a record pace.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s07.mp3",
     "dur": 12.168,
     "start": 2134,
     "end": 2500
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_08.jpg",
   "start": 2504,
   "end": 2813,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "In the first half of the year, the Air Force logs more new reports than in the previous four years combined. Project Blue Book is overwhelmed.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s08.mp3",
     "dur": 9.216,
     "start": 2514,
     "end": 2791
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_09.jpg",
   "start": 2795,
   "end": 3002,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And the capital's air traffic control center is about to have the strangest shift of its career.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s09.mp3",
     "dur": 5.808,
     "start": 2805,
     "end": 2980
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "I \u00b7 NIGHT ONE",
    "The First Night",
    "JULY 19 \u00b7 1952"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_10.jpg",
   "start": 2984,
   "end": 3387,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item one. Saturday night, July nineteenth. Just before midnight, controller Edward Nugent sees seven unidentified targets about fifteen miles south-southwest of the city.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s10.mp3",
     "dur": 12.36,
     "start": 2994,
     "end": 3365
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_11.jpg",
   "start": 3369,
   "end": 3659,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "They drift slowly, then lurch ahead at speeds that seem impossible. His senior controller checks the set. It's working normally.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s11.mp3",
     "dur": 8.568,
     "start": 3379,
     "end": 3637
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_12.jpg",
   "start": 3641,
   "end": 4012,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Radar at the national airport sees them too. And radar at Andrews Air Force Base. Three separate sets, three separate rooms, the same unknown objects.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s12.mp3",
     "dur": 11.28,
     "start": 3651,
     "end": 3990
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_13.jpg",
   "start": 3994,
   "end": 4314,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "At Andrews, an airman looks up and sees an orange ball with a tail, streaking across the sky. This is no longer just a blip on a screen.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s13.mp3",
     "dur": 9.576,
     "start": 4004,
     "end": 4292
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_14.jpg",
   "start": 4296,
   "end": 4616,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A Capital Airlines pilot reports six white lights shooting past his plane over fourteen minutes. Tower controllers see a hovering light, too.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s14.mp3",
     "dur": 9.6,
     "start": 4306,
     "end": 4594
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_15.jpg",
   "start": 4598,
   "end": 4931,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Then the moment that chills the controllers. An object sits right over a radio beacon, and on all three radars it vanishes at the same instant.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s15.mp3",
     "dur": 10.032,
     "start": 4608,
     "end": 4909
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_16.jpg",
   "start": 4913,
   "end": 5313,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Around three in the morning, two F-94 jets arrive from Delaware. As they approach, the blips disappear. When the jets run low on fuel and leave, the targets come back.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s16.mp3",
     "dur": 12.24,
     "start": 4923,
     "end": 5291
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_17.jpg",
   "start": 5295,
   "end": 5599,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The last target fades around five-thirty, with the sunrise. Nobody in the radar room has any doubt something strange has happened.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s17.mp3",
     "dur": 9.048,
     "start": 5305,
     "end": 5577
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "II \u00b7 THE PENTAGON",
    "Ruppelt Hears",
    "JULY 20 \u00b7 1952"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_18.jpg",
   "start": 5581,
   "end": 5873,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item two. The man in charge of Project Blue Book, Captain Edward Ruppelt, learns about all of it from the Monday headlines.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s18.mp3",
     "dur": 8.64,
     "start": 5591,
     "end": 5851
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_19.jpg",
   "start": 5855,
   "end": 6163,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "He tries to get a staff car and fly back. He can't. For the next week, the official investigation is a phone call away from the story.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s19.mp3",
     "dur": 9.168,
     "start": 5865,
     "end": 6141
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_20.jpg",
   "start": 6145,
   "end": 6496,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "One officer already suggests the answer. Weather can bend radar beams and create false targets. Remember that idea. It becomes the official line.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s20.mp3",
     "dur": 10.608,
     "start": 6155,
     "end": 6474
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "III \u00b7 NIGHT TWO",
    "The Second Saturday",
    "JULY 26 \u00b7 1952"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_21.jpg",
   "start": 6478,
   "end": 6757,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item three. Saturday, July twenty-sixth. A second Saturday. A second flap. This time, the whole city is watching.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s21.mp3",
     "dur": 8.208,
     "start": 6488,
     "end": 6735
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_22.jpg",
   "start": 6739,
   "end": 7020,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "At eight-fifteen in the evening, a National Airlines crew sees lights. Radar picks the same targets up almost at once.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s22.mp3",
     "dur": 8.28,
     "start": 6749,
     "end": 6998
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_23.jpg",
   "start": 7002,
   "end": 7342,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Blue Book's press officer is at the airport. Reporters are crowding the radar rooms. Some of the targets are said to move at seven thousand miles an hour.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s23.mp3",
     "dur": 10.248,
     "start": 7012,
     "end": 7320
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_24.jpg",
   "start": 7324,
   "end": 7669,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "At eleven-thirty, jets are scrambled again. Captain John McHugo sees nothing. But Lieutenant William Patterson sees four white glows, and gives chase.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s24.mp3",
     "dur": 10.416,
     "start": 7334,
     "end": 7647
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_25.jpg",
   "start": 7651,
   "end": 7987,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "His words, as reported: I see them now, and they're all around me. He turns, they slip away. He calls off the chase when the lights seem to surround him.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s25.mp3",
     "dur": 10.128,
     "start": 7661,
     "end": 7965
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_26.jpg",
   "start": 7969,
   "end": 8379,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Two experienced officers, Major Dewey Fournet and Navy Lieutenant John Holcomb, watch the scopes. They judge the returns good and solid. A weak inversion, they say, can't explain them.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s26.mp3",
     "dur": 12.576,
     "start": 7979,
     "end": 8357
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_27.jpg",
   "start": 8361,
   "end": 8464,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The lights end at sunrise. Again.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s27.mp3",
     "dur": 2.352,
     "start": 8371,
     "end": 8442
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "IV \u00b7 THE PRESS",
    "The Press Conference",
    "JULY 29 \u00b7 1952"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_28.jpg",
   "start": 8446,
   "end": 8731,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item four. The White House is paying attention. President Truman's air aide asks the Air Force what on Earth is going on.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s28.mp3",
     "dur": 8.424,
     "start": 8456,
     "end": 8709
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_29.jpg",
   "start": 8713,
   "end": 8986,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "On July twenty-ninth, two generals face the press. The largest Pentagon press conference since the Second World War.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s29.mp3",
     "dur": 8.016,
     "start": 8723,
     "end": 8964
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 30,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_30.jpg",
   "start": 8968,
   "end": 9347,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "General John Samford says the Air Force has had credible observers report relatively incredible things. Then he says the answer is probably temperature inversions.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s30.mp3",
     "dur": 11.544,
     "start": 8978,
     "end": 9325
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_31.jpg",
   "start": 9329,
   "end": 9734,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "An inversion is a layer of warm air over cool air. It can bend a radar beam back to the ground and show a ghost target. It's a real effect. The question is whether it fits.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s31.mp3",
     "dur": 12.432,
     "start": 9339,
     "end": 9712
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 32,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": [
    "V \u00b7 CROSS-EXAMINATION",
    "Weather or Not?",
    "EVIDENCE TABLE"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_32.jpg",
   "start": 9716,
   "end": 9970,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item five. The cross-examination. Let's weigh the evidence for each explanation, starting with the inversion.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s32.mp3",
     "dur": 7.392,
     "start": 9726,
     "end": 9948
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_33.jpg",
   "start": 9952,
   "end": 10332,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "For the inversion: a government weather study finds one in almost every one of the nights in question. A famous astronomer, Donald Menzel, and sceptic Philip Klass back it.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s33.mp3",
     "dur": 11.592,
     "start": 9962,
     "end": 10310
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_34.jpg",
   "start": 10314,
   "end": 10698,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "For the sceptics, one radar target was traced to a steamboat on the Potomac, heading for Mount Vernon. Many of the visual sightings were stars, meteors, and aircraft lights.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s34.mp3",
     "dur": 11.712,
     "start": 10324,
     "end": 10676
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_35.jpg",
   "start": 10680,
   "end": 11075,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Klass adds that early radar was prone to false targets, and that later digital filters wiped many of them away. He called the controllers two dumb operators. That's a harsh take.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s35.mp3",
     "dur": 12.072,
     "start": 10690,
     "end": 11053
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_36.jpg",
   "start": 11057,
   "end": 11385,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Against it: the controllers were not new. Some had years of experience, and they said these returns were hard and sharp. Not the fuzzy clutter they knew.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s36.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 11067,
     "end": 11363
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_37.jpg",
   "start": 11367,
   "end": 11654,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And the radar matched what people saw with their eyes. Howard Cocklin, decades later: I saw it on the screen and out the window.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s37.mp3",
     "dur": 8.496,
     "start": 11377,
     "end": 11632
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_38.jpg",
   "start": 11636,
   "end": 11986,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Three independent radars. Pilots in the air. Witnesses on the ground. An inversion can fool one set. Fooling everything at once is a harder sell.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s38.mp3",
     "dur": 10.584,
     "start": 11646,
     "end": 11964
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_39.jpg",
   "start": 11968,
   "end": 12330,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Even a later university study could not settle it. A physicist said witnesses still disputed the weather explanation. Jacques Vall\u00e9e called the case rather poor.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s39.mp3",
     "dur": 10.992,
     "start": 11978,
     "end": 12308
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 40,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": [
    "VI \u00b7 THE THEORY",
    "The Alien Theory",
    "TESTED"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_40.jpg",
   "start": 12312,
   "end": 12587,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item six. The alien theory. Visitors from another world, scouting the capital of the most powerful nation on Earth.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s40.mp3",
     "dur": 8.088,
     "start": 12322,
     "end": 12565
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 41,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_41.jpg",
   "start": 12569,
   "end": 12837,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Why would they come two weeks in a row, then vanish? Why show up only as lights and radar blips, never land, never speak?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s41.mp3",
     "dur": 7.848,
     "start": 12579,
     "end": 12815
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 42,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_42.jpg",
   "start": 12819,
   "end": 13227,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "What the evidence does show is a loop. Headlines drove sightings. Sightings drove headlines. Sixteen thousand newspaper items ran in about a hundred and fifty papers that year.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s42.mp3",
     "dur": 12.504,
     "start": 12829,
     "end": 13205
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 43,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_43.jpg",
   "start": 13209,
   "end": 13456,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Once the story was in every paper, every star became a saucer, and every controller was watching for one.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s43.mp3",
     "dur": 7.152,
     "start": 13219,
     "end": 13434
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 44,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_44.jpg",
   "start": 13438,
   "end": 13695,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And that's where the story takes a darker turn. Because the government was just as worried about the panic as the lights.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s44.mp3",
     "dur": 7.488,
     "start": 13448,
     "end": 13673
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 45,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "VII \u00b7 THE COVER-UP",
    "The CIA Steps In",
    "SEP 1952 \u2013 JAN 1953"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_45.jpg",
   "start": 13677,
   "end": 14072,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item seven. September, nineteen fifty-two. A CIA memo warns that floods of saucer reports could jam military channels, and might even spark mass hysteria.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s45.mp3",
     "dur": 12.096,
     "start": 13687,
     "end": 14050
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 46,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_46.jpg",
   "start": 14054,
   "end": 14362,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "In January nineteen fifty-three, a panel of scientists meets for four days. They review the best cases, and watch the famous films.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s46.mp3",
     "dur": 9.192,
     "start": 14064,
     "end": 14340
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_47.jpg",
   "start": 14344,
   "end": 14672,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Their conclusion: nothing threatens national security, but the public interest does. The cure? Debunk the sightings, and strip the aura of mystery.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s47.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 14354,
     "end": 14650
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 48,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_48.jpg",
   "start": 14654,
   "end": 15023,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Blue Book shifts. It starts explaining cases away, and it stops publicising the ones it can't. The Washington flap changed how the government talks about UFOs.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s48.mp3",
     "dur": 11.232,
     "start": 14664,
     "end": 15001
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 49,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": [
    "VIII \u00b7 SCORECARD",
    "Four Claims",
    "SCORED"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_49.jpg",
   "start": 15005,
   "end": 15208,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Item eight. The scorecard. Three claims, tested against what we can actually verify.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s49.mp3",
     "dur": 5.688,
     "start": 15015,
     "end": 15186
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 50,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_50.jpg",
   "start": 15190,
   "end": 15506,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Claim one. Radar saw unknown targets. Verified. Multiple operators, multiple radars, multiple nights, in official records.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s50.mp3",
     "dur": 9.456,
     "start": 15200,
     "end": 15484
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 51,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_51.jpg",
   "start": 15488,
   "end": 15852,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Claim two. Pilots and controllers saw lights in the same places. Partly verified. Real reports exist, but many lights match stars, meteors and planes.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s51.mp3",
     "dur": 11.064,
     "start": 15498,
     "end": 15830
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 52,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_52.jpg",
   "start": 15834,
   "end": 16145,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Claim three. An inversion explains everything. Not proven. It likely explains many targets, but no study ever matched every sighting.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s52.mp3",
     "dur": 9.288,
     "start": 15844,
     "end": 16123
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 53,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_53.jpg",
   "start": 16127,
   "end": 16443,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Claim four. Aliens did it. Unsupported. There is no physical evidence, no photo, no wreckage. Only lights, scopes, and stories.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s53.mp3",
     "dur": 9.456,
     "start": 16137,
     "end": 16421
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 54,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": [
    "IX \u00b7 VERDICT",
    "Unresolved",
    "THE FINDING"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_54.jpg",
   "start": 16425,
   "end": 16753,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The verdict. Unresolved, but leaning weather. The inversion is a strong candidate, but the people in the room never accepted it, and nobody can prove it.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s54.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 16435,
     "end": 16731
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 55,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_55.jpg",
   "start": 16735,
   "end": 17048,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "What we can say for certain: the Air Force and the CIA took the sky seriously, the press took it more seriously, and the public never forgot.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s55.mp3",
     "dur": 9.36,
     "start": 16745,
     "end": 17026
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 56,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_56.jpg",
   "start": 17030,
   "end": 17335,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Today, radar is digital and filtered. And the odd thing is, nobody has reported a night like July nineteen fifty-two since.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s56.mp3",
     "dur": 9.072,
     "start": 17040,
     "end": 17313
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 57,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_57.jpg",
   "start": 17317,
   "end": 17541,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "If the lights were weather, the weather has never repeated it. If they were something else, they haven't returned either.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s57.mp3",
     "dur": 6.384,
     "start": 17327,
     "end": 17519
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 58,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_58.jpg",
   "start": 17523,
   "end": 17775,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "So what do you think was in the sky over Washington? Weather, or something we still can't name? Tell us in the comments.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s58.mp3",
     "dur": 7.32,
     "start": 17533,
     "end": 17753
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 59,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_59.jpg",
   "start": 17757,
   "end": 18017,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Next case: a night in Iran, nineteen seventy-six, when two jets chased a light, and one of them lost every system.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s59.mp3",
     "dur": 7.584,
     "start": 17767,
     "end": 17995
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 60,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_60.jpg",
   "start": 17999,
   "end": 18091,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Subscribe for the next case file.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s60.mp3",
     "dur": 1.968,
     "start": 18009,
     "end": 18069
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}